1
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:07,130
It's amazing people keep coming to comic book stores

2
00:00:07,140 --> 00:00:10,200
instead of just downloading comics digitally.

3
00:00:10,610 --> 00:00:12,140
It's probably for the best.

4
00:00:12,140 --> 00:00:14,210
For a lot of these guys, the weekly trip here

5
00:00:14,210 --> 00:00:16,280
is the only chance their mom has to go down

6
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:18,110
to the basement and change their sheets.

7
00:00:19,980 --> 00:00:23,320
Oh, that reminds me, I get fresh sheets tonight. Yay.

8
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:26,920
Well?

9
00:00:26,920 --> 00:00:28,820
What do you think of New Comic Book Night?

10
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:31,320
Magic, huh?

11
00:00:31,530 --> 00:00:33,230
Sheldon, I'm disappointed.

12
00:00:33,230 --> 00:00:34,430
As a brilliant man,

13
00:00:34,430 --> 00:00:35,600
you're entitled to a vice.

14
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:37,300
I could understand frequenting an opium den

15
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:39,430
or hunting your fellow man for sport.

16
00:00:40,670 --> 00:00:44,000
But this? Lame-o.

17
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:48,610
Well, A) Comic books employ storytelling through sequential art,

18
00:00:48,610 --> 00:00:50,740
an medium that dates back 17,000 years

19
00:00:50,750 --> 00:00:52,610
to the cave paintings of Lascaux,

20
00:00:52,610 --> 00:00:54,950
and B) You play the harp.

21
00:00:54,950 --> 00:00:56,550
Like that's cool.

22
00:00:59,720 --> 00:01:02,020
Can I help you find anything?

23
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:04,120
A comic that depicts a woman whose bosom

24
00:01:04,130 --> 00:01:06,190
can't be used as a flotation device.

25
00:01:07,130 --> 00:01:08,660
Sorry. Most of the guys

26
00:01:08,660 --> 00:01:10,900
who come in here like big boobs.

27
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:13,070
Couple of them have big boobs.

28
00:01:14,440 --> 00:01:17,900
The new Warlords of Ka'a expansion pack is out.

29
00:01:17,910 --> 00:01:20,040
A new one? Unbelievable.

30
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:22,340
They just keep making up more cheesy monsters,

31
00:01:22,340 --> 00:01:25,780
slapping them on cards and selling them at 25 bucks a pop.

32
00:01:25,780 --> 00:01:29,320
It's like a secret tax on guys who can't get laid.

33
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:31,490
They're not even trying.

34
00:01:31,490 --> 00:01:33,620
Remember the Satanimals pack with the Hellephant?

35
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:34,990
Why, absurd.

36
00:01:34,990 --> 00:01:37,460
What was he, a bad elephant who died and went to hell?

37
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:39,860
What could an elephant possibly do

38
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:42,200
that would cause him eternal damnation?

39
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:43,830
"Wild West and Witches"?

40
00:01:43,830 --> 00:01:47,030
What kind of loser cares about a showdown

41
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:50,900
between Billy the Kid and the White Wizard of the North?

42
00:01:50,910 --> 00:01:52,440
A total loser.

43
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:54,470
Obviously, a guy with a six-shooter

44
00:01:54,480 --> 00:01:56,340
beats an old man with a magic wand.

45
00:01:57,980 --> 00:01:59,610
Well, h-hold on.

46
00:02:00,820 --> 00:02:02,580
Uh, what if the wizard casts

47
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:05,790
a Helmet of Confusion spell on Billy the Kid's cowboy hat?

48
00:02:05,790 --> 00:02:07,250
What? Please!

49
00:02:07,260 --> 00:02:09,090
This is Billy the Kid we're talking about.

50
00:02:09,090 --> 00:02:10,960
I mean, the wizard would get shot between the eyes

51
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:12,190
before he could ever get out the words,

52
00:02:12,190 --> 00:02:13,330
"What the hell is Billy the Kid doing

53
00:02:13,330 --> 00:02:16,100
in the mystic realm of Ka'a?"

54
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:18,400
Leonard...

55
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:21,400
What's the deal with Sheldon's friend Amy?

56
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:22,570
Are they a couple?

57
00:02:22,670 --> 00:02:24,940
Couple of weirdos. Why?

58
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:26,840
You interested in Amy?

59
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:29,510
Well, I mean, she didn't look through me

60
00:02:29,510 --> 00:02:31,310
with soul-sucking, ball-shriveling

61
00:02:31,310 --> 00:02:33,880
hatred and contempt.

62
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:35,820
I like that in a woman.

63
00:02:37,090 --> 00:02:39,490
Could you run it by Sheldon if I could ask her out?

64
00:02:39,490 --> 00:02:40,820
Sure. I guess.

65
00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:43,220
Stuart, settle an argument for us.

66
00:02:43,220 --> 00:02:44,290
Who would win,

67
00:02:44,290 --> 00:02:46,630
Billy the Kid or the White Wizard?

68
00:02:46,630 --> 00:02:48,600
If I tell you that,

69
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:51,800
I'm robbing you of the hours of fun you could have

70
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:57,100
for the magical, rootin'-tootin' low price of $24.95.

71
00:02:57,770 --> 00:02:59,240
I'll take one.

72
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:00,770
Mm... make it two.

73
00:03:00,780 --> 00:03:03,480
I hate all of you and myself. Three.

74
00:03:04,610 --> 00:03:06,650
I'll ring it up.

75
00:03:06,950 --> 00:03:09,550
Like shooting nerds in a barrel.

76
00:03:35,350 --> 00:03:37,620
Hey, can I talk to you about something?

77
00:03:37,620 --> 00:03:40,190
It's a little awkward.

78
00:03:40,190 --> 00:03:42,420
I know what this is about.

79
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:45,220
Given the professional standstill you're at,

80
00:03:45,230 --> 00:03:47,660
you're wondering if this is the appropriate time

81
00:03:47,660 --> 00:03:51,230
to abandon your research and focus on teaching.

82
00:03:54,770 --> 00:03:56,900
Yes.

83
00:03:57,740 --> 00:03:59,540
And if I may suggest,

84
00:03:59,540 --> 00:04:01,140
consider changing disciplines.

85
00:04:01,140 --> 00:04:03,410
Yeah, to the humanities-- perhaps history.

86
00:04:03,410 --> 00:04:05,840
One of the advantages of teaching history

87
00:04:05,850 --> 00:04:08,550
is that you don't have to create things.

88
00:04:08,550 --> 00:04:11,580
You know, you just have to remember stuff that happened

89
00:04:11,590 --> 00:04:13,490
and then parrot it back.

90
00:04:13,690 --> 00:04:15,690
You could have fun with that.

91
00:04:17,060 --> 00:04:18,660
Yeah, that's not it.

92
00:04:18,660 --> 00:04:21,090
Stuart's kind of interested in Amy.

93
00:04:21,100 --> 00:04:23,500
Oh, of course he is. She's very interesting.

94
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:25,630
Did you know, when she was 14,

95
00:04:25,630 --> 00:04:28,730
she severed the webbing between her own toes?

96
00:04:30,470 --> 00:04:32,340
No.

97
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:34,540
He wanted me to find out

98
00:04:34,540 --> 00:04:37,740
if you'd have a problem with him asking her out.

99
00:04:39,410 --> 00:04:42,510
I'm not sure how to respond, Leonard.

100
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:44,980
I don't own Amy.

101
00:04:44,990 --> 00:04:47,620
Can't own a person.

102
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:50,360
At least not since...

103
00:04:54,430 --> 00:04:56,660
1863.

104
00:04:58,030 --> 00:05:00,870
President Lincoln freed the...

105
00:05:02,200 --> 00:05:04,840
Slaves! Come on, Leonard,

106
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:05,710
if you're going to teach history,

107
00:05:05,710 --> 00:05:08,140
these are the kind of facts you'll have to know.

108
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:10,110
You know what? Never mind.

109
00:05:10,110 --> 00:05:12,240
I'm going to tell him it's okay to ask her out.

110
00:05:12,250 --> 00:05:13,550
The question is moot.

111
00:05:13,550 --> 00:05:15,410
There is no way that Stuart,

112
00:05:15,420 --> 00:05:17,580
an impoverished peddler of picture books,

113
00:05:17,590 --> 00:05:20,250
would be at all appealing to Amy Farrah Fowler,

114
00:05:20,250 --> 00:05:22,360
a noted neurobiologist

115
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:25,090
capable of performing surgery on her own feet

116
00:05:25,090 --> 00:05:27,330
with nothing but nitrous oxide

117
00:05:27,330 --> 00:05:29,960
from cans of whipped cream as anesthesia.

118
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:33,100
All right, but for the record,

119
00:05:33,100 --> 00:05:36,000
I checked in with you to see how you'd feel about it.

120
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:38,500
Fine. The record shall so reflect.

121
00:05:38,510 --> 00:05:41,210
Now, getting back to the problem at hand,

122
00:05:41,210 --> 00:05:44,510
what to do with a washed-up experimental physicist...

123
00:05:46,550 --> 00:05:48,650
I am not washed-up.

124
00:05:48,650 --> 00:05:50,620
Oh, Leonard.

125
00:05:50,620 --> 00:05:53,990
Lots of people love you and want to help you,

126
00:05:53,990 --> 00:05:57,090
but they can't until you admit the problem.

127
00:05:59,830 --> 00:06:02,460
Well, ladies, we killed the bottle.

128
00:06:02,460 --> 00:06:03,730
I had half a glass.

129
00:06:04,230 --> 00:06:06,870
- I didn't have any. - Okay, don't judge me.

130
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:09,700
So, what do you want to do--

131
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:12,910
go to the movies, go dancing, lay down for a little bit?

132
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:18,740
Or we play... Travel Twister.

133
00:06:19,510 --> 00:06:21,910
Amy, really? Twister?

134
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:25,020
Excuse me. I've passed many an enjoyable evening playing this game.

135
00:06:25,020 --> 00:06:26,720
And I'm sure it's a lot more exciting

136
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:28,820
when you play with other people.

137
00:06:30,490 --> 00:06:32,760
What do you say, bestie? We can do shirts and skins.

138
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:34,230
I'm shirts. Called it.

139
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:39,270
I'm too small for Twister.

140
00:06:39,470 --> 00:06:40,870
And roller coasters.

141
00:06:40,870 --> 00:06:43,440
And sitting with my feet on the floor.

142
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:48,240
Hope you enjoyed the prenatal cigarettes, Mom.

143
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:53,320
Hey, you know, my mom smoked pot when she was pregnant with me,

144
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:55,110
and I turned out just fine.

145
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:56,450
Hey, look, I have peach schnapps.

146
00:06:56,450 --> 00:06:57,690
Thank God.

147
00:06:59,090 --> 00:07:00,950
Guys, something happened.

148
00:07:00,950 --> 00:07:01,950
What's wrong?

149
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:04,460
I think a boy likes me.

150
00:07:05,530 --> 00:07:07,130
"Hi. It's Stuart.

151
00:07:07,130 --> 00:07:09,060
"We met at the comic book store.

152
00:07:09,060 --> 00:07:11,500
"I was wondering if you'd like to get coffee sometime.

153
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:12,830
"It's okay if you say no.

154
00:07:12,830 --> 00:07:14,500
"It might be the kick in the pants I need

155
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:16,440
to start taking Zoloft."

156
00:07:18,340 --> 00:07:20,470
Amy, little vixen.

157
00:07:20,470 --> 00:07:23,980
Just working it under all those layers of wool and polyester.

158
00:07:25,340 --> 00:07:26,450
What are you going to do?

159
00:07:26,450 --> 00:07:28,010
Doesn't he know you have a boyfriend?

160
00:07:28,020 --> 00:07:29,280
Oh, she doesn't have a boyfriend;

161
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:31,120
she has a Sheldon.

162
00:07:31,520 --> 00:07:33,690
So do you like Stuart?

163
00:07:33,690 --> 00:07:35,050
I don't know.

164
00:07:35,060 --> 00:07:36,360
He's nice.

165
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:37,520
He's funny.

166
00:07:37,530 --> 00:07:39,120
He has the sallow, drawn countenance

167
00:07:39,130 --> 00:07:41,060
associated with an overactive thyroid gland.

168
00:07:41,060 --> 00:07:42,800
That's kind of hot.

169
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:45,760
Okay, look, sweetie, we all love Sheldon,

170
00:07:45,770 --> 00:07:47,770
but you've been with him over a year now.

171
00:07:47,770 --> 00:07:48,870
If it's not going anywhere,

172
00:07:48,870 --> 00:07:50,470
what does it hurt to look around?

173
00:07:50,470 --> 00:07:53,810
Well, yeah, I guess they're not engaged like me and Howie.

174
00:07:53,810 --> 00:07:54,840
Yeah, for what it's worth,

175
00:07:54,840 --> 00:07:56,110
engaged people can look around, too.

176
00:07:56,110 --> 00:07:57,610
Lot of options out there.

177
00:08:07,090 --> 00:08:08,650
Where's Stuart?

178
00:08:09,860 --> 00:08:11,390
Out.

179
00:08:12,830 --> 00:08:14,160
Who are you?

180
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,330
I'm Dale.

181
00:08:15,330 --> 00:08:17,400
He left me in charge.

182
00:08:20,130 --> 00:08:21,100
Really?

183
00:08:21,100 --> 00:08:22,130
Yeah.

184
00:08:22,140 --> 00:08:24,200
I don't get it, either.

185
00:08:27,140 --> 00:08:28,320
I want to return this

186
00:08:28,320 --> 00:08:31,480
"Wild West and Witches Ka'a" expansion pack.

187
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:33,350
Sorry. I don't do returns.

188
00:08:33,350 --> 00:08:34,910
They're hard.

189
00:08:36,380 --> 00:08:38,180
Sure, sure.

190
00:08:39,290 --> 00:08:41,020
Uh, when will Stuart be back?

191
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:42,790
I don't know. He went out for coffee.

192
00:08:42,790 --> 00:08:44,420
With a girl.

193
00:08:46,830 --> 00:08:49,060
Oh, I guess I was wrong.

194
00:08:50,030 --> 00:08:51,400
You okay?

195
00:08:52,370 --> 00:08:53,870
Am I okay?

196
00:08:53,870 --> 00:08:56,170
Leonard, I'm on a lifelong trajectory

197
00:08:56,170 --> 00:08:59,170
that includes a Nobel Prize and cities named after me,

198
00:08:59,170 --> 00:09:00,640
all four wisdom teeth

199
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:02,910
fit comfortably in my mouth without need of extraction,

200
00:09:02,910 --> 00:09:06,250
and my bowel movements run like a German train schedule.

201
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:10,780
Am I okay?

202
00:09:11,850 --> 00:09:13,490
I'm okay, too!

203
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:23,680
Wild Bill Witchcock.

204
00:09:25,780 --> 00:09:28,590
A tribe of Abra-Comanches.

205
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:35,890
Flaming Spittoon.

206
00:09:35,890 --> 00:09:36,790
And for the record,

207
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:39,130
I'm very disappointed in you cowpokes.

208
00:09:39,530 --> 00:09:42,530
We're playing our inaugural round of "Wild West and Witches" ,

209
00:09:42,530 --> 00:09:43,620
and I'm the only one

210
00:09:43,620 --> 00:09:45,270
who bothered to dress for the occasion.

211
00:09:46,370 --> 00:09:48,040
Patooie.

212
00:09:49,110 --> 00:09:51,370
We're not wearing cowboy hats, Sheldon.

213
00:09:51,380 --> 00:09:52,910
It looks ridiculous.

214
00:09:52,910 --> 00:09:57,250
And I suppose my boots and spurs are ridiculous, too?

215
00:09:57,250 --> 00:09:59,620
- Yeah.  - Very.  - Incredibly so.

216
00:09:59,620 --> 00:10:03,150
Did it look ridiculous when we got the Satanimals pack

217
00:10:03,160 --> 00:10:06,920
and I dressed up as a Beelzebobcat?

218
00:10:06,930 --> 00:10:08,630
- Yeah.  - Very.  - Incredibly so.

219
00:10:10,290 --> 00:10:12,160
All right, fine. Let's just play.

220
00:10:12,160 --> 00:10:13,830
We should go easy on him.

221
00:10:13,830 --> 00:10:15,630
Amy's out with Stuart tonight.

222
00:10:15,630 --> 00:10:16,770
Wait a minute.

223
00:10:16,770 --> 00:10:19,670
Are you telling me that Sheldon's patented blend

224
00:10:19,670 --> 00:10:21,870
of condescension and no sex

225
00:10:21,870 --> 00:10:24,240
isn't enough to hold on to a woman?

226
00:10:28,310 --> 00:10:29,410
Cluck, cluck, cluck.

227
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:30,780
What are we, ladies at a quilting bee?

228
00:10:30,780 --> 00:10:33,720
Or are we men playing a fantasy card game

229
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:36,420
set in a magical frontier town?

230
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:39,660
Sorry.

231
00:10:39,860 --> 00:10:42,360
Creepy Tepee.

232
00:10:43,530 --> 00:10:45,930
Annie Ogly.

233
00:10:48,470 --> 00:10:51,300
Hocus Pocus Pocahontas.

234
00:10:51,300 --> 00:10:54,070
And may I point out it is the three of you

235
00:10:54,070 --> 00:10:56,510
who are obsessed with Stuart and Amy, not me.

236
00:10:56,510 --> 00:10:58,110
I think you need to ask yourselves

237
00:10:58,110 --> 00:11:00,080
who's really being ridiculous here.

238
00:11:08,690 --> 00:11:10,590
- It's you.  - You are.  - Totally you.

239
00:11:13,190 --> 00:11:14,520
Hey, guys, check it out.

240
00:11:14,530 --> 00:11:16,560
The deluxe limited edition "Wild West and Witches"

241
00:11:16,560 --> 00:11:20,100
expansion pack in the signed and numbered collector's tin.

242
00:11:20,100 --> 00:11:21,530
Come on, no!

243
00:11:21,530 --> 00:11:24,130
We just bought the regular pack.

244
00:11:24,140 --> 00:11:25,470
Ooh, a sheriff's badge.

245
00:11:27,240 --> 00:11:29,110
Yeah, it's also a wand.

246
00:11:31,040 --> 00:11:34,240
With a hologram? Nice!

247
00:11:34,250 --> 00:11:35,750
Hey, do you see this?

248
00:11:35,750 --> 00:11:38,380
I'm in the matrix, Leonard; I see everything.

249
00:11:38,380 --> 00:11:40,280
You got to be kidding me.

250
00:11:40,290 --> 00:11:42,350
You friended Stuart on Facebook?

251
00:11:42,350 --> 00:11:44,190
I thought you didn't like Facebook anymore.

252
00:11:44,190 --> 00:11:45,260
Don't be silly.

253
00:11:45,260 --> 00:11:47,230
I'm a fan of anything that tries to

254
00:11:47,230 --> 00:11:48,930
replace actual human contact.

255
00:11:49,730 --> 00:11:51,430
Please.

256
00:11:51,430 --> 00:11:53,930
You're looking at Facebook to find out how their date went.

257
00:11:53,930 --> 00:11:55,270
Really?

258
00:11:55,270 --> 00:11:57,030
You think I care if a man, what,

259
00:11:57,040 --> 00:12:00,870
"shared a pumpkin latte with a dynamite lady"?

260
00:12:00,870 --> 00:12:01,940
You're so full of it.

261
00:12:01,940 --> 00:12:05,610
You are free to believe whatever you like.

262
00:12:05,610 --> 00:12:08,850
And unfriend Rajesh Koothrappali.

263
00:12:08,850 --> 00:12:10,410
You unfriended me? Seriously?

264
00:12:10,420 --> 00:12:11,780
Oh, yeah.

265
00:12:11,780 --> 00:12:13,680
Now he's gonna miss all those great updates like,

266
00:12:13,690 --> 00:12:15,390
"I can't believe I waited this long

267
00:12:15,390 --> 00:12:17,290
to make my own potpourri"

268
00:12:18,860 --> 00:12:20,420
Sheldon, why don't you just acknowledge

269
00:12:20,430 --> 00:12:21,760
that you have feelings for Amy

270
00:12:21,760 --> 00:12:23,960
and you don't want her going out with other men?

271
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:27,700
And unfriend Leonard Hofstadter.

272
00:12:27,700 --> 00:12:28,830
Here's a radical thought.

273
00:12:28,830 --> 00:12:31,200
Go old-school, challenge Stuart to a fight.

274
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:32,800
I mean, nothing makes the ladies hotter

275
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:34,740
than two skinny white guys

276
00:12:34,740 --> 00:12:37,010
swatting at each other with their eyes closed.

277
00:12:39,540 --> 00:12:41,610
And unfriend Howard Wolowitz.

278
00:12:42,650 --> 00:12:43,650
That's all of us.

279
00:12:43,650 --> 00:12:45,580
- Can I use the laptop?  - Why?

280
00:12:45,580 --> 00:12:49,290
I have to buy that stupid collector's tin.

281
00:12:50,910 --> 00:12:52,910
- Who do we love?  - Penny.

282
00:12:52,910 --> 00:12:54,340
- Who do we love?  - Penny.

283
00:12:54,350 --> 00:12:56,880
- Who do we love?  - Penny.

284
00:12:57,280 --> 00:12:58,650
Hello, Sheldon.

285
00:12:58,650 --> 00:12:59,880
Come on in.

286
00:12:59,880 --> 00:13:02,450
- Thank you.  - What's up?

287
00:13:02,450 --> 00:13:06,720
I came to ask if you would like to go on a date with me.

288
00:13:08,860 --> 00:13:10,930
I'm sorry, what?

289
00:13:10,930 --> 00:13:12,230
A date.

290
00:13:12,230 --> 00:13:13,360
You and me.

291
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:15,060
Dining, dancing,

292
00:13:15,070 --> 00:13:18,030
perhaps you'd like to take in a prizefight.

293
00:13:18,970 --> 00:13:21,770
God, are you trying to make Amy jealous?

294
00:13:21,770 --> 00:13:23,040
No.

295
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:26,040
Why is everyone so obsessed with Amy and Stuart?

296
00:13:26,040 --> 00:13:28,280
Whether or not they may be having more pumpkin lattes

297
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:30,280
or intercourse tonight.

298
00:13:30,280 --> 00:13:32,950
Okay, listen to me.

299
00:13:32,950 --> 00:13:35,950
Playing games is not gonna help get Amy back.

300
00:13:35,950 --> 00:13:38,190
I am not trying to get her back.

301
00:13:38,190 --> 00:13:41,460
But, out of curiosity, what is a way?

302
00:13:41,460 --> 00:13:43,490
All right, honey, let me tell you a story.

303
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:46,660
There was a guy I liked, and I never told him how I felt.

304
00:13:46,660 --> 00:13:48,830
Eventually, he started going out with someone else,

305
00:13:48,830 --> 00:13:50,830
and I always regretted it.

306
00:13:50,840 --> 00:13:52,970
Do you see where I'm going with this?

307
00:13:52,970 --> 00:13:54,600
I believe I do.

308
00:13:55,870 --> 00:13:57,870
I'm the guy.

309
00:14:01,210 --> 00:14:02,710
You're not the guy.

310
00:14:02,710 --> 00:14:04,610
Are you sure?

311
00:14:04,620 --> 00:14:06,480
That would explain so much.

312
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:09,050
Your constant presence in my apartment,

313
00:14:09,050 --> 00:14:11,850
that baffling dalliance with Leonard just to be near me,

314
00:14:11,860 --> 00:14:15,220
the way you call me "sweetie" all the time.

315
00:14:15,230 --> 00:14:16,490
I call everyone "sweetie."

316
00:14:16,490 --> 00:14:17,660
You tramp.

317
00:14:20,700 --> 00:14:22,060
Look, Sheldon, all I'm saying is

318
00:14:22,070 --> 00:14:24,240
strap on a pair and go talk to Amy.

319
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:26,170
"Strap on a pair"?

320
00:14:26,170 --> 00:14:29,110
Of what, skates?

321
00:14:30,710 --> 00:14:33,410
Oh, sweetie, you are so not the guy.

322
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:42,220
If you're bored, you can go.

323
00:14:42,220 --> 00:14:44,820
I understand.

324
00:14:45,220 --> 00:14:47,890
No, I'm having a nice time.

325
00:14:48,490 --> 00:14:50,690
Don't patronize me.

326
00:14:52,700 --> 00:14:54,630
Excuse me. Excuse me.

327
00:14:54,630 --> 00:14:55,700
Pardon me.

328
00:14:56,770 --> 00:14:58,330
Pardon me. Excuse me.

329
00:14:58,340 --> 00:14:59,330
Hi, Stuart.

330
00:14:59,340 --> 00:15:00,170
Hi, Sheldon.

331
00:15:00,170 --> 00:15:02,070
Pardon me... Excuse me...

332
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:08,780
Sheldon, what are you doing here?

333
00:15:08,780 --> 00:15:11,580
The thought of you sitting in a darkened theater

334
00:15:11,580 --> 00:15:14,820
with a character like Stuart is repellent.

335
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:18,020
No offense, Stuart.

336
00:15:18,020 --> 00:15:19,590
None taken.

337
00:15:19,590 --> 00:15:23,360
Although "repellent" is kind of a... kind of a strong word.

338
00:15:26,700 --> 00:15:29,500
I'm sorry this causes you discomfort,

339
00:15:29,500 --> 00:15:32,260
but based on the currently established parameters of our relationship,

340
00:15:32,260 --> 00:15:35,640
I can put myself in any repellent situation I want.

341
00:15:35,640 --> 00:15:37,470
Um, again...

342
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:39,680
Stuart, please. You're being rude.

343
00:15:41,950 --> 00:15:44,380
Anything else?

344
00:15:44,380 --> 00:15:50,950
I believe I would like to alter the paradigm of our relationship.

345
00:15:52,620 --> 00:15:54,490
I'm listening.

346
00:15:54,490 --> 00:15:59,300
With the understanding that nothing changes whatsoever,

347
00:15:59,300 --> 00:16:01,160
physical or otherwise,

348
00:16:01,170 --> 00:16:03,770
I would not object to

349
00:16:03,770 --> 00:16:09,400
us no longer characterizing you as "not my girlfriend."

350
00:16:14,610 --> 00:16:17,080
Interesting.

351
00:16:17,080 --> 00:16:20,150
Now try it without the quadruple negative.

352
00:16:20,150 --> 00:16:23,550
You're being impossible.

353
00:16:23,550 --> 00:16:25,620
Hi, Stuart.

354
00:16:27,660 --> 00:16:30,660
Fine.

355
00:16:30,660 --> 00:16:34,000
Amy...

356
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:37,230
will you be my girlfriend?

357
00:16:44,040 --> 00:16:46,240
- Yes.  - Well, that's enough of that.

358
00:16:48,080 --> 00:16:49,580
Sorry to interrupt.

359
00:16:49,580 --> 00:16:51,550
You two enjoy your date.

360
00:16:51,550 --> 00:16:53,280
Here's a dollar for your troubles.

361
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:55,350
Get yourself some Sour Patch Kids.

362
00:16:55,350 --> 00:16:57,220
Excuse me... Excuse me... Pardon me...

363
00:17:01,090 --> 00:17:05,030
So, other than you taking your relationship

364
00:17:05,030 --> 00:17:09,070
to the next level with another guy, this was nice.

365
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:13,240
Yes, well, thanks for seeing me to my door.

366
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:14,600
Oh, you're welcome.

367
00:17:14,610 --> 00:17:18,310
Amy. Amy. Amy.

368
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:23,110
Let's wrap things up out there.

369
00:17:26,780 --> 00:17:28,750
Um, good night, Stuart.

370
00:17:28,750 --> 00:17:29,620
Good night.

371
00:17:32,260 --> 00:17:33,290
Take the hint, Stuart.

372
00:17:33,290 --> 00:17:35,360
The lady said "Good night."

373
00:17:38,960 --> 00:17:41,060
How did you get into my apartment?

374
00:17:41,070 --> 00:17:43,670
Is that the kind of nagging I can expect

375
00:17:43,670 --> 00:17:45,330
